        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "WHIpv",
          "name": "Flow J · List total — outside plan vs from plan",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 28,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "K3mz28",
              "name": "Flow Header",
              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": 6,
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "Tnjer",
                  "name": "Title",
                  "fill": "$color/text",
                  "content": "J · List total — outside plan vs from plan",
                  "fontFamily": "$font/family",
                  "fontSize": 30,
                  "fontWeight": "700"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "NyJoL",
                  "name": "Desc",
                  "fill": "$color/text-secondary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": 1100,
                  "content": "List lens only — Month and Plan keep their own header. From plan = expenses a Fixed PlanItem created (planItem != nil) + expenses whose category sits in an active envelope of that cycle's plan (PlanOrigins). Outside plan = everything else. Plan is violet everywhere: header segment and every row tag (filled ☑ Plan = Fixed, outlined 📥 <envelope> = envelope). Rows outside the plan carry no tag. The split only appears in a cycle that has a plan. Option C (daily as the hero) was rejected — see 05 · Proposals.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.4,
                  "fontFamily": "$font/family",
                  "fontSize": 16,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "v0si2E",
              "name": "Screens",
              "gap": 64,
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "oLXDi",
                  "name": "Column A",
                  "width": 402,
                  "layout": "vertical",
                  "gap": 16,
