                  "content": "S · Paying ahead — an expense counts in a later cycle's envelope",
                  "fontFamily": "$font/family",
                  "fontSize": 30,
                  "fontWeight": "700"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "ICTyu",
                  "name": "Desc",
                  "fill": "$color/text-secondary",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": 1300,
                  "content": "docs/prd/envelope-assignment.md §4.10, ADR-0009. Built 14 Oct 2026, no schema change. Payday is the 25th; November's plan (25 Oct – 24 Nov) holds Travelling for a trip on the 27th, and on 14 Oct the owner buys the ticket. An expense may now be assigned to an active envelope of any LATER cycle whose plan exists and has not ended — paid early. It keeps its date: in its own cycle it stays in the list and the total, Outside plan, in no envelope, with a dashed violet tag “Travelling · Nov”. The later envelope counts it in its bar, remainder and drift, with a caption “Rp 1.200.000 paid early in October”. Never backward; no plan is ever created to have somewhere to pay into; no schema change (Expense.envelope already exists). One sample (§7.1, -seedPlanData paid-early): the normal October plan, plus November carried over with Travelling Rp 2.000.000; Tiket KAI ke Jakarta, Transport Rp 1.200.000, 14 Oct → Travelling: Rp 800.000 left. On device, the ＋ stays level with the bar when the caption is drawn, and the picker, the Move sheet and the long-press item all read one offer (EnvelopeOffer).",
                  "lineHeight": 1.4,
                  "fontFamily": "$font/family",
                  "fontSize": 16,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
            },
