              "fontFamily": "$font/family",
              "fontSize": 30,
              "fontWeight": "700"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "X41FOX",
              "name": "Desc",
              "fill": "$color/text-secondary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 1300,
              "content": "docs/prd/envelope-assignment.md §8.1, ADR-0009. Not drawn as frames — each was rejected before design. (1) Change the expense's date into the envelope's cycle: the ledger would lie about when the money left. (2) Mark it No envelope and lower next cycle's envelope by hand: two edits that drift apart, and the bar never shows the ticket. (3) A Fixed item in the current cycle's plan: it plans in October money budgeted for November. Built instead: (4) an assignment may point forward to a later cycle's envelope. Also not chosen at grilling: offering only the next cycle (owner override — every later open cycle is offered); a Paid-early section in the next cycle's List lens (the envelope row's caption was chosen).",
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "fontFamily": "$font/family",
              "fontSize": 16,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
